infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Same logic, two plans: the pre-PG12 CTE optimization fence
  desc Why "CTE vs subquery" was substance, not style — the planner treated them differently
  compares
    - label CTE before PostgreSQL 12
      children
        - label Unconditional optimization fence
          desc Planner evaluates the CTE separately and never looks through it
        - label Materialized whole
          desc The full result is built first, then the outer query filters it
        - label No predicate pushdown
          desc Outer WHERE tenant_id = 7 cannot reach inside — scans far more rows
        - label Sometimes dramatically slower
          desc Millions of rows materialized before a single filter applies
    - label Inline subquery in FROM
      children
        - label No fence
          desc Planner flattens the subquery into the outer query
        - label Predicates push down
          desc WHERE tenant_id = 7 reaches the underlying table
        - label Index-aware filtering
          desc Chooses an index and reads only the matching rows
        - label Same default since PG12
          desc NOT MATERIALIZED now inlines a CTE the same way
theme
  palette #f43f5e #6366f1
